  "summary": "Ukrainian Art Nouveau, also known as Ukrainian Architectural Modern (UAM; Ukrainian: Український архітектурний модерн, Неоукраїнський стиль), is an architectural style which emerged during the first decade of the 20th century in connection with the rise of the Ukrainian national movement.",
  "description": "Ukrainian Art Nouveau, also known as Ukrainian Architectural Modern (UAM; Ukrainian: Український архітектурний модерн, Неоукраїнський стиль), is an architectural style which emerged during the first decade of the 20th century in connection with the rise of the Ukrainian national movement. Based on folk traditions of house and church construction, as well as examples of Ukrainian Baroque architecture and European Art Nouveau, the style retained prominent positions in Ukrainian architecture for almost 40 years.",
  "culturalContext": "The UAM is based on the forms of Ukrainian folk house and church architecture. In this regard, it is worth noting that for the first time, elements of Ukrainian folk architecture began to be used by professional architects back in the 19th century (e.g., Galagan's House in Lebedyntsi).",
